## The architectural intent (what the specs say after the rewrite)

1. **Hooks docs are a prose edit.** A new Hooks section in the docs, made directly by the orchestrator, no pipeline. User: "the hooks is a simple fix you just add a new section to the docs".
2. **Observer page needs design + content decision first.** A design pass and a decision with the user on what goes on the page, before any spec or plan. User: "the observer page needs a design pass and we need to decide what actually goes on the page".
3. **Research runs in a separate brain session.** Uses the brain's research skill, per the user.
4. **Hooks docs ship from the package as `.aide/docs/hooks/index.md`. — SUPERSEDED by #20** User chose the folder option: the aidemd-mcp repo adds `hooks/index.md` under its `.aide/docs/`, registered in `src/service/install/initContent/index.ts` (`DOC_PATHS` + `METHODOLOGY_DOCS`, `hostFilename: "hooks/index.md"`), updates the methodology-doc count test (`initContent/index.test.ts`, currently 13), adds a line to `.aide/docs/index.md` and an `[Unreleased]` changelog entry; release via `release-check` then `scripts/publish.mjs`; then `/aide:upgrade` on the site. The site adds a fifth `DOCS_CATEGORIES` entry after Skills with root `.aide/docs/hooks` and excludes that subfolder from the methodology walk (a `src/service/docsRegistry` change, whose spec currently says four roots). User also wants it in the sidebar under Skills.
5. **Observer page is a standalone /observer page.** A custom page like `/brain`, with a top-bar link, linked from the Hooks doc. User approved this outline: (1) What it is: a local live view of every agent session on your machine, one per user. (2) The problem it solves: two agent sessions colliding in one project, sessions that silently stall, no visibility into which pipeline phase is running. (3) How it works: hooks report working/waiting/ended, sessions report pipeline events, one open session per project (HALT/BLOCKED/end session), the pipeline rail, 'maybe stuck' after 15 quiet minutes. (4) Benefits. (5) Reference: ports, AIDE_OBSERVER_PORT, data folder per OS. A design pass is still required (user: 'the observer page needs a design pass').
6. **SEO/AEO target queries, in priority order.** 1. 'intent driven engineering' / 'intent-driven development' — definition page + glossary, definition in first paragraph, short FAQ. 2. 'spec-driven development vs intent-driven development' — comparison page. 3. 'spec-kit alternatives' / 'spec-kit vs openspec' — honest comparison page with dated stars and feature table (spec-kit, OpenSpec, BMAD, superpowers, Kiro, Tessl, Agent OS, Task Master). 4. 'claude code subagents pipeline' — how-to guide through spec→research→plan→build→QA; Hooks and Observer pages belong here. 5. 'mcp server for development workflow' — install quickstart + MCP directory listings. 6. 'open source agentic sdlc framework' — explainer mapping pipeline stages to SDLC phases, with FAQ. Do not target bare 'spec driven development' or 'agentic sdlc'. Citation levers with strongest evidence: crawler-readable static pages, headings in the searcher's exact wording, answer early, visible update dates, third-party mentions. Schema markup and FAQ markup showed no reliable lift; keep llms.txt (coding agents read it). Always pair 'AIDE' with 'intent-driven' or 'aidemd' (name collision with another 'AIDE' project and the Linux IDS).
7. **Naming: keep both names, fix metadata.** User chose to keep `aidemd-mcp/server` and `@aidemd-mcp/server` and apply the research's GitHub/npm metadata fixes (About text, website field, `spec-driven-development` topic, README first paragraph as a plain definition, npm homepage/description/keywords, describe the `aidemd.dev` repo, describe or archive `aidemd.dev-v1`). Implementation moved to the aidemd-mcp repo as task `github-npm-and-mcp-registry-discovery-metadata` (user, 2026-11-26: 'the GitHub change seems to be an MCP repository task. Make that task on the Kanban board. I don't want you doing it from here.').
8. **Observer page goes through a Claude Design handoff first.** User: 'we need to create a design handoff for this'. Brief at `design-handoff/observer/brief.md` asks Claude Design for two variants (A Explainer linear scroll; B Live mock of the observer) in the same handoff shape as `design-handoff/handoff.md` (/brain). Once the handoff returns, it is implemented with the `design-handoff` skill.
9. **Proposed /observer tree (architect, structure mode — pre-handoff; superseded: a fresh structure proposal is made against Variant A's sections before the spec).** `src/app/observer/` with one `.aide`; `page.tsx` orchestrator (metadata, skip-link, `<TopBar sticky active="observer" />`, `<main id="main">`, `<Footer />`); `_components/` one helper folder per section: Hero, Problem, HowItWorks, Benefits, Reference, HooksCrossLink; `_data/observerCopy/index.ts`; no layout.tsx; server components by default; no imports from `src/app/brain/_components`. TopBar (`NAV_LINKS`, `ActivePage`, path label) and `src/app/sitemap.ts` (`/observer/` with trailing slash, playbook-conformant lastModified) go in a separate root-scope plan in `.aide/`. Conflicts to realign first: `.aide/intent.aide` pins nav to six destinations and lists brain as forbidden (already stale vs shipped docs·brain·github·npm); `src/app/brain/.aide` pins nav to exactly four and forbids a fifth; root names only landing+docs as surfaces; root 'never drift from the package' vs hand-written reference values; root 'forest green #3d6b4a only accent' vs state colours. Spec order: realign root → realign brain → observer `.aide` → design → plans.
10. **/observer page copy comes from research.** User: 'the architect shouldnt have proposed wording it needs to be derived from research and filled in appropriately'. The section wording in decision #9's tree and in the first `design-handoff/observer/brief.md` is placeholder, not approved copy. Page structure and copy are derived from the page-design research (which now also covers content and messaging) and written into the rewritten brief.
11. **Observer page positioning and shape (from research, founder-approved).** Lead with what Anthropic's `claude agents` view lacks: the pipeline rail, one open session per project (HALT/BLOCKED), one local web view across projects; the three states come after. Product-first, ~500–1,000 words, real-UI capture on the first screen (staged with demo projects, no private data), one hero action repeated at the bottom. State visual system: shape + word + colour, green = live only, one warning colour, four colours scoped to /observer. Avoid 'dashboard' and 'stuck' as headings; use 'monitor … sessions', 'waiting for you'. Variants: A capture-led stack, B annotated capture.
12. **Confirmed public facts (founder-verified 2026-11-25).** MIT, open source; no telemetry, no account; local, read-only, 127.0.0.1 behind a token; one observer per user covering every project; Windows, macOS, Linux; hooks are Claude Code only and AIDE install/upgrade wires them (no extra config); no desktop notifications.
13. **Observer capture uses the aidemd.dev theme, no caption.** The /observer page shows the real observer components and demo data restyled into the site theme (dark #0d0b08, JetBrains Mono, forest green), via a CSS override injected at capture time; the live observer keeps its own, more legible theme. User: 'we don't need that caption'. This settles the state-legend colour question: the page uses the site palette, matching its own capture.
14. **The page calls it 'the observer'.** Founder decision (2026-11-25). The capture's UI header still reads 'AIDE Pipeline Viewer'; page copy never uses that name. Recorded in `design-handoff/observer/brief.md` §1.
15. **`#6aaa7c` is the site green for text.** Founder (2026-11-25): 'Yes, same green'. The lightened `#6aaa7c` (same hue as `#3d6b4a`, which is 3.18:1 as text) is the site green wherever green is text or an icon; `#3d6b4a` stays for fills. It does not breach the root spec's 'no second green' rule. Recorded in `design-handoff/observer/brief.md` §5.
16. **Ship Variant A of the v2.1 /observer handoff.** Ship Variant A (capture-led stack) of the v2.1 /observer handoff (design-handoff/observer/observer-variant-capture-stack.jsx), per the user on 2026-11-26. Variant B (annotated capture) is not built.
17. **The /observer install line is `npx -y @aidemd-mcp/server@latest init`** (user, 2026-11-26), replacing the handoff's [INSTALL COMMAND — TO CONFIRM] placeholder (O2.install) in the hero, the closing panel and the copy button. The HALT/BLOCKED agent-reply snippets use the server's real reply format (recorded under What's already done, 2026-11-26 explorer), filled with the capture's demo data. Both replacements are applied in the build, from this record; the handoff files in design-handoff/observer/ stay as exported.
18. **Ship the Variant A copy as drafted; the founder reviews it live.** User (2026-11-26): 'go with whatever ill review it once its live'. All 10 DRAFT lines ship as worded in design-handoff/observer/observer-shared.jsx and the DRAFT markers are removed. Two lines change only where they misstate a fact: Local and private drops the claim that the access token keeps data local (it is the 127.0.0.1 binding; the token guards who can open the page), and the 'starts with it at 127.0.0.1:24680' line is hedged because the port moves up to 24689 when 24680 is taken. Design's state colours stand (maybe stuck grey #948e82, BLOCKED red #ff5f56). <title>/OG text as Claude Design wrote them ('the observer · AIDEMD.DEV', description = the subhead); OG image stays the hero capture for now. Placeholder links (#hooks, github, npm) get the real targets in the build.
19. **/observer tree approved (user, 2026-11-26), with the site TopBar + Footer.** `src/app/observer/` gets one `.aide`, no layout.tsx. `page.tsx` thin server orchestrator: metadata (title absolute 'the observer · AIDEMD.DEV', description = subhead, canonical/og:url https://aidemd.dev/observer/, OG image = hero capture 1440×1180), imports `./observer.css` (handoff observer.css copied value-for-value, scoped by `.o2`), skip-link, `<TopBar sticky active="observer" />`, `<main id="main">` [Hero, CaptureFigure, Sections, ClosePanel], site `<Footer />`. `_data/observerCopy/index.ts`: the O2 copy object (decisions #17/#18 applied; the founder edits wording here). `_components/`: Hero (+FactList); CaptureFigure (CaptureImage, StateLegend); Sections (PipelineRail, OneSessionPerProject + AgentReply, WorkingWaitingEnded, HowItKnows, QuietFifteen, LocalAndPrivate, Setup; Sections/shared: SectionBlock, CodeText); ClosePanel; shared: StateLabel (+StateIcon), InstallBox (+CopyButton, the only client component). Captures copied byte-identical to `public/observer/` (hero and rail, 1x/2x), plain `<img srcSet>`. Not ported: Variant B, pins, RailDemo, DRAFT markers, `.ph` tags, the handoff's O2Nav/drawer and O2Foot, the session capture. User chose the site TopBar + Footer over the handoff's own nav/footer, so the nav and footer are excluded from the pixel diff and brain's no-hamburger rule is untouched. Root-scope plan in `.aide/`: `src/data/navLinks/index.ts` shared roster; TopBar gets `observer` in `ActivePage`, the `/observer` entry after brain, the `/observer` path label; `src/app/sitemap.ts` adds `/observer/`; `src/types/observer/index.ts`. Decision #9's tree is superseded by this one.
20. **Hooks docs are site-owned, not shipped by the package (supersedes decision #4). — SUPERSEDED by #22** User (2026-11-26): 'i dont think the mcp server needs to include docs... if the ui isn't including them its a ui fix no?' The site adds a Hooks section to the docs sidebar after Skills. Its event list is read at build time from `.claude/settings.json` (written by `/aide:upgrade`), so it updates with the package; a short explanation (what each event sets — working/waiting/ended — that hooks print nothing and never block the agent, that AIDE's install wires them) is written in the site and must match the aidemd-mcp source. No aidemd-mcp release needed. Built in this pipeline; the /observer Setup 'Hooks — full reference in the docs →' link points at it.
21. **Root and brain spec realignment confirmed (user, 2026-11-26).** `.aide/intent.aide`: description covers custom guide and feature pages; nav on every page is docs, brain, observer, github ↗, npm ↗; each route is pixel-checked at 1440px against its own handoff; forest green is the only accent (#3d6b4a fills, #6aaa7c text/icons) with /observer's state colours page-scoped; hand-written values on custom pages match the @aidemd-mcp/server source. `src/app/brain/.aide`: exactly five nav entries incl. observer; no-hamburger rule kept. User also approved cleaning the stale six-/seven-entry nav text in both bodies.
22. **Hooks docs ship from aidemd-mcp in a new `.aide/reference/` folder (supersedes #20).** User (2026-11-26): an agent in this project should not author the hooks docs; the MCP ships them, but not in `.aide/docs/` (methodology only) and not in `.claude/hooks/` (reserved for Claude). aidemd-mcp adds `.aide/reference/`: `.aide/tools.md` moves there and is split for progressive disclosure (`tools/index.md` = table of contents only, one file per tool, missing tools added), plus `reference/hooks/` in the same format (index table + one file per event). It ships to projects via init/upgrade. Tracked as aidemd-mcp task `add-aide-reference-folder-destructure-tools-add-hooks` (Backlog, p1). After it releases, the site runs /aide:upgrade and adds the reference folders as docs roots; until then the /observer Setup 'Hooks — full reference in the docs →' link points at /docs/. No site-owned Hooks page or settings.json table is built. Implemented in the specs as decision #27.
23. **`observer` stays visible in the mobile TopBar** (user, 2026-11-26): mobile row shows docs, brain, observer; github ↗ and npm ↗ hide as today. The brain spec's line that brain is the only nav link beyond docs surviving mobile collapse must be updated.
24. **/observer spec confirmed (user, 2026-11-26).** `src/app/observer/.aide` frontmatter-only, research no / strategy no; outcomes fold handoff §10 (Variant A, nav/footer and Variant B lines dropped) and are pixel-checked at 1280 and 390 against the Variant A artboards with the site TopBar/Footer excluded. The root spec now pixel-checks each route at its own handoff's design widths (landing/docs 1440). Brain spec mobile line: brain survives mobile collapse alongside docs and observer.
25. **Build waits for the aidemd-mcp reference release** (user, 2026-11-26: 'wait for the mcp to ship the new reference docs'). Both plans are written and stay `proposed`, not approved: `.aide/plan.aide` (root, 7 steps: vitest include + qa-artifacts in .gitignore; src/types/observer; src/data/navLinks; TopBar observer entry, mobile-visible; sitemap /observer/ with git lastModified; globals.css `--font-mono: var(--font-jetbrains-mono), "JetBrains Mono", ui-monospace, monospace` font fix; captures copied to public/observer/) and `src/app/observer/plan.aide` (7 steps: scoped observer.css; observerCopy; observerMetadata; shared pieces with CopyButton the only client component; Hero/CaptureFigure/ClosePanel; seven sections + AgentReply; page.tsx). After `add-aide-reference-folder-destructure-tools-add-hooks` ships in aidemd-mcp: /aide:upgrade the site, then the architect revises the plans to add the reference folders as docs roots (docsRegistry, llmsTxt, root specs need updating first) and point the /observer Hooks link at the real hooks reference, then the user approves. Release landed 2026-11-26 (0.19.0); the wait is over.
26. **Plan-review answers (user, 2026-11-26).** HALT snippet's Observer link shortened to `?token=…` (no real-looking token on the page). Regenerate the tests/visual/ 1440 goldens after the font fix (intended change). Copy strings flagged for the founder's live review: then-line 'then run /aide — the observer starts with it, usually at 127.0.0.1:24680'; Local and private 'It serves on 127.0.0.1, so your session data stays on your machine; an access token guards who can open it. No telemetry, no account. It’s read-only: it can’t change a session.'
27. **Docs reference roots: two sections, no counts (user, 2026-11-26).** `.aide/reference/tools/` and `.aide/reference/hooks/` become two new docs content roots, each its own docs-sidebar section after Skills; section order methodology, commands, agents, skills, tools, hooks (tools before hooks — offered to the user, not objected to); URLs /docs/tools/<slug> and /docs/hooks/<slug>; /llms.txt gets one H2 per docs section in the same order. User chose "Drop exact counts": specs pin no page counts. Frontmatter of `.aide/intent.aide`, `src/service/docsRegistry/.aide` and `src/service/llmsTxt/.aide` updated and approved by the user; their bodies fixed by the strategist to match (six roots, no counts), approved by the user (2026-11-26). Code not yet changed: `src/data/docsCategories.ts` (DOCS_CATEGORIES, SECTION_INDEX_META, its "four roots … skills last" comment) and the DocSection type need `tools` and `hooks`.
28. **In-doc links resolve to live routes; a broken one fails the build (user, 2026-11-26).** Relative links between docs render as the target doc's route (no .md, correct section, across content roots, trailing slash), resolved by file path through the registry, never by string-munging. A relative .md link whose target does not exist prints a build warning naming the link and its doc and is left as written; the build passes (user: "Warn, leave link as is"). Specified in src/service/docsRegistry/.aide. The upstream fix shipped in 0.19.1 (commit d8b9c2e); a full render of the 67 docs now prints zero warnings.
29. **Only the URL is lowercased (user, 2026-11-26).** User chose "Lowercase all doc URLs", then on the architect's `fileSlug` proposal: "Can't we just lowercase the href?" — so each doc keeps its real name (slug in the file's case, e.g. `Stop`, `aide/SKILL`) for labels and titles; only the URL is lowercased: urlPath, the generated static route params, and every rendered link to it (/docs/hooks/stop/). No `fileSlug` field. The docsRegistry spec and all four plans now follow this: slug in file case; urlPath lowercase; pages addressed by urlPath; within a section index first, then by lowercased URL path; getByKey compares case-insensitively; cite-as uses the lowercased path.
30. **Old mixed-case skills URLs may 404 (user, 2026-11-26).** /docs/skills/<name>/SKILL becomes …/skill; GitHub Pages cannot redirect; user: "Accept the change".
31. **Tools and Hooks section names and subtitles (user, 2026-11-26).** Sidebar/heading titles are "Tools" and "Hooks"; section-index subtitles (ledes) "the MCP tools @aidemd-mcp/server exposes" and "the Claude Code hook events AIDE listens to" approved.
32. **1440 goldens re-baselined to the current site (user, 2026-11-26).** User: "Regenerate all three". The new goldens include accumulated drift from earlier shipped changes, not just this cycle. og.png re-render discarded ("Restore to committed version").
33. **Monospace fallback face matches JetBrains Mono metrics (2026-11-26, fix loop).** next/font's default Arial fallback is replaced by a local "JetBrains Mono Fallback" face (0.6em advance) so out-of-subset glyphs render monospace and the hero headline does not re-wrap on font swap.
34. **Reduced motion shows the finished headline (2026-11-26).** Under prefers-reduced-motion the hero typewriter renders the full headline with no timers; normal-motion visitors keep the looping reveal. The caret remounts per typing step so the hero has zero layout shift.
35. **SEO/AEO scope (user, 2026-11-26).** All six decision-#6 pages are built, in the research's priority order — the user wants the brain SEO/AEO research to decide ('every single piece'). Copy: 'Draft from research, I review' — drafted from the brain research notes under research/seo-aeo/, marked draft, kept in a per-page data module, the founder reviews. Design: 'Reuse existing site chrome' — no Claude Design handoff; site TopBar + Footer. Site-wide SEO fixes: 'Yes, include it' — titles/meta, headings in searchers' wording, visible updated dates, sitemap stops stamping build time and drops priority. GitHub/npm metadata (#7) stays a separate item.
