- 2026-11-26 explorer (aidemd-mcp, read-only): install command is `npx -y @aidemd-mcp/server@<version> init` from the project root (README.md:36 pins @0.18.0); init installs the server globally itself (`npm i -g @aidemd-mcp/server`) and writes the .mcp.json entry as the global `aidemd-mcp` command, so the npx timeout concern does not apply to the one-shot init. Manual route: `npm i -g @aidemd-mcp/server` then `claude mcp add aide -- aidemd-mcp`. HALT reply (src/tools/observer/start/formatReply): first line 'HALT: another session of this project is open. Nothing proceeds until the user approves ending it with aide_observer_end_session, or closes this session.', then one line per open session '- <name> · <working | waiting on the user> · <active | quiet N min[, maybe stuck]> · last activity <ISO time> · pipeline <name|none> · phase <phase|none>', then 'Observer: <link>'. BLOCKED reply: 'BLOCKED: the observer could not start, so nothing proceeds. <reason>', e.g. 'No port could be bound: 24680 (in use), … 24689 (in use)'. Observer binds 127.0.0.1, default port 24680 walking up to 24689; the printed link is http://127.0.0.1:<port>/p/<project>/s/<session>?token=<token>.
